note The window and the event loop, and the only place this program blocks. winit owns the loop; the app is one trait built around one method, frame (the other two answer a test script), so nothing above here knows what a window event is. The loop is not a game loop: it waits for events and redraws only when input arrived or a timer the last frame asked for came due, so an idle codemap costs one frame a second. Every event does the same two things - update the accumulated Input and mark the frame pending - and the redraw turns that Input into one frame and clears it.

