note The test script: before each frame, lines run until one produces input or waits, and that input reaches the app exactly as a real event would. click, dblclick and drag expand into their own frames - a double click is a press carrying the count, since the press is the frame the app sees it on - and the -id forms look the element up by name first, hover landing on a bare mouse move. dump prints the frames since the previous dump - how many, the worst, how many over 16 ms - before the app adds its own state, so a script measures a hitch without the app knowing anything about time. Unknown lines are the app's own commands.

